# Containment Protocol — Implementation Lite Rules

Read `docs/agent-operating-manual.md` before substantive work. This tracked entry point remains always applied; the manual supplies the shared procedure. Do not run full backlog hygiene unless requested.

## Source of truth and scope

Read the issue, comments, parent/children, linked evidence, and slice doc. Linear owns approved scope and lifecycle; GitHub supplies implementation evidence. Follow `docs/cursor-autonomous-authority.md` for Cursor; ChatGPT phase gates do not bind Cursor. Keep the active PR within its verified boundary. Prefer existing systems and owners; no speculative frameworks, unrelated cleanup, or child-only parent closure.

## Pre-coding summary and audit

Apply manual §§2–3: report files, current/expected behavior, boundary, status, risks, checks and docs before edits. Repeat all six pre-ship passes after fixes; run required validation. Record deferrals durably with the correct existing owner or candidate route. Do not weaken tests or claim unrun checks passed.

## Ship loop and Linear

Apply manual §4: commit → push → PR using `.github/pull_request_template.md` → independent full-diff review → external-review/CI fixes → merge → sync main. Link the actual slice and approved covered children; post PR and merge evidence on the existing owner. Keep active owned implementation In Progress until full acceptance ships; assess parent completion independently. Honor explicit no-commit/push/PR/merge or local/plan-only instructions.

## Session closeout

Use `docs/agent-session-closeout.md` phase A while blocked/open, phase B after merge. No next-issue coding, candidate reconciliation, or delegated selection in merge closeout. At most plan an already-approved next issue for a new session. Cursor retains autonomous selection on a later authorized continuation.

Use `docs/cloud-agent-linear-handoff.md` only on its approved-implementation-completed-and-merged trigger when Linear was not updated. Docs-only pending traceability follows manual §4; read-only sessions use `docs/read-only-session-handoff.md`.
